# Financial Friday v0.5.0 Sprint – Advisor Intelligence

## Sprint Objective

Version **0.5.0** marks the transition from building a financial application to building an intelligent financial advisor.

The primary objective of this sprint is **not** to add new user-facing features. Instead, this sprint establishes the architectural and philosophical foundation that will guide all future development.

Every design and engineering decision should support the mission of creating the world's most trusted AI financial advisor.

---

# Sprint Goals

## 1. Finalize Product Documentation

Complete the foundational documents that define Financial Friday.

### Deliverables

- Final Constitution
- Vision & Mission
- Advisor Intelligence Specification
- Technical Blueprint

---

## 2. Audit the Existing Codebase

Perform a complete review of the current application.

### Review Areas

- Project structure
- Folder organization
- Existing screens
- Firebase integration
- Authentication
- Routing
- State management
- Current dependencies
- Technical debt
- Opportunities for refactoring

### Deliverable

- Codebase Audit Report

---

## 3. Refine Project Architecture

Ensure the existing architecture supports long-term scalability.

### Review Areas

- Data flow
- Backend architecture
- Firebase services
- Security model
- Data models
- API boundaries
- AI integration strategy

### Deliverable

- Architecture Approval

---

## 4. Advisor Intelligence Design

Translate the 43 completed philosophical decisions into technical behavior.

### Define

- Recommendation engine
- Confidence model
- Priority engine
- Emergency Mode
- Financial Story
- Memory model
- Trend analysis
- Goal management
- Notification logic
- Transparency system

### Deliverable

- Advisor Intelligence Specification

---

## 5. Prepare for Implementation

Before adding major functionality, ensure the project is technically ready.

### Tasks

- Resolve technical debt
- Improve project organization
- Remove obsolete code
- Improve documentation
- Confirm development workflow
- Establish coding standards

### Deliverable

- Implementation Ready

---

# Success Criteria

The sprint is considered complete when:

- All foundational documentation is complete.
- The project architecture has been reviewed and approved.
- The Advisor Intelligence behavior has been fully specified.
- The codebase is organized for scalable development.
- The project is ready to begin implementing the Advisor.

---

# Guiding Principles

During this sprint we will prioritize:

- Simplicity
- Scalability
- Transparency
- Maintainability
- Security
- User Trust
- Long-term Thinking

Every engineering decision should support the principles established in the Financial Friday Constitution.

---

# Out of Scope

The following items are intentionally excluded from this sprint unless required by the architecture:

- New dashboard features
- New budgeting tools
- Investment calculators
- Additional UI polish
- Marketing pages
- Performance optimization beyond architectural needs

The focus of Version **0.5.0** is building the foundation, not expanding functionality.

---

# Definition of Done

Version **0.5.0** is complete when Financial Friday has transitioned from a collection of application features into a well-defined platform with a documented architecture, an intelligent advisor design, and a scalable foundation capable of supporting future development.

---

# Sprint Motto

> **"Build the foundation once. Build the future on top of it."**
